      "empirical_finding": "Domestic USA buyers spend \u20b941,024.10 (+3.34%) more on average than international buyers (mean \u20b912,69,852.05 vs \u20b912,28,827.94; Welch's t=2.2443, p=0.0251, Cohen's d=0.1181). Investment share is statistically indistinguishable between USA (30.56%, 470/1538) and international buyers (31.39%, 145/462) with chi2=0.1139 (p=0.7358, dof=1). International buyers do NOT form a distinct higher-spend investor cluster.",
      "statistical_test": "Chi-Square Independence (USA vs Intl Investment Purpose): chi2=0.1139, p=0.7358, dof=1; Spend Comparison: Welch's t=2.2443, p=0.0251, Cohen's d=0.1181; Mann-Whitney U p=0.0094",
