      "empirical_finding": "Company clients represent 5.15% (103 clients) of dataset. Crucially, companies do NOT purchase significantly more units than individuals: company mean is 3.70 units vs individual mean of 3.65 units (one-way ANOVA F(1, 1998)=0.3333, p=0.5638; two-sample t(1998)=-0.5773, p=0.5638; Kruskal-Wallis H=0.1855, p=0.6667). Corporate designation does not drive multi-unit volume.",
